Walking 12 minutes to reach the famous Ribeira district, a charming riverside restaurant area, and Bridge D. Luis.

This apartment, located on the second floor, blends the charm of history with modern comfort. The reconstruction preserved the elegance of the period, offering you a luxurious and welcoming retreat with an exclusive location: its windows open onto the Carmo and Carmelite Churches.
Historical and design highlights:
Original wooden staircase;
Central skylight: ensures abundant natural light;
Crafted stucco ceiling;
Windows with rose windows: add a touch of distinction.

